Specification checks: exactly 12 dark semantic color roles; DEPR logo authority; 48dp minimum touch targets; 12sp monospace hashes/addresses; body >=14sp; dynamic layouts at 200% text scale. Operational layouts remain flat obsidian. Gradient button decoration requires a solid contrast-qualified label area unless every fill position passes AA.

Implementation status: NOT_RUN for screenshots, accessibility tree, keyboard navigation, screen readers, font scaling, visual geometry approval and device layouts. Concept references are not passing implementation evidence. line is decorative; muted/cyan boundaries require measured component contrast. Light palette uses accessible #167B56 mint rather than source #1F8A62 for small white CTA labels.
