Display cardHash never authorizes wallet bytes. messageSha256 hashes exact parsed serialized message excluding signatures; immutable copies/reparse and contextHash bind account/cluster/genesis/policy/evidence/time/fee. Legacy and v0 static-key messages are supported; unresolved lookups fail closed. Mainnet submission is disabled; real devnet/device qualification and full deployment validation remain prerequisites.

Canonical manifest profile is RFC 8785 string/bool/null/array/object subset, with numeric JSON values forbidden. Integer counters/timestamps remain strings. Golden vectors confirm cross-language key order and Unicode/newline preservation. Legacy receipt migration and legacy signHash contracts remain incomplete rather than reinterpreted.

Node key signatures use software Ed25519 control identity, not wallet/Keystore identity. Hardware evidence signatures require qualified reported levels and independent envelope verification. Node counters are local measurements, not peer corroboration/rewards. The gnark sample is blocked on dependencies and has no generated proof; no hash or receipt substitutes for cryptographic proof generation.

Qualification levels stay false while build/device/full scope remain incomplete. Test results are scope-specific; no device/protocol check inherits PASS from a synthetic fixture. Licensing for new source is proposed MIT; imported asset rights unresolved. No publishing/deployment/mainnet spending/token issuance.
